01:13:14,870 --> 01:13:22,709
which will capture signals across the sound and electromagnetic spectrum beyond the visible audible range, right?

905
01:13:22,709 --> 01:13:28,790
It will gain the ability to sense things that we can't like, you know, things.

906
01:13:28,790 --> 01:13:34,310
that are invisible, inaudible to us, things we might not be able to smell or taste.

907
01:13:34,310 --> 01:13:39,910
And that opens up extraordinary possibilities which is to some extent scary.

908
01:13:39,910 --> 01:13:46,149
because they will be able to perceive the world at a level much beyond our own capacities.

909
01:13:46,159 --> 01:13:48,550
Pretty scary.

910
01:13:48,550 --> 01:13:53,510
And I think that's something that we all have to watch out for of what the world brings.

911
01:13:53,510 --> 01:13:56,390
to us with all this innovation.

912
01:13:56,390 --> 01:13:59,590
I want to end the show by asking you a question.

913
01:13:59,590 --> 01:14:05,510
Every day there seems to be a new innovation, a newer way of doing things.

914
01:14:05,510 --> 01:14:09,350
So how to keep up with this fast pace of innovation?

915
01:14:09,360 --> 01:14:17,590
Oh yeah, that's so pertinent and honestly it is difficult for all of us and you know.

916
01:14:17,590 --> 01:14:19,990
I I do find the pace of innovation very dizzying.

917
01:14:19,990 --> 01:14:25,350
because there's just so much happening with new tools, new models, new papers.

918
01:14:25,350 --> 01:14:31,270
It literally feels like you are at the receiving end of a fire hose.

919
01:14:31,270 --> 01:14:33,590
So I have my coping mechanisms and I'm sure everybody does.

920
01:14:33,600 --> 01:14:36,470
So I could definitely share these.

921
01:14:36,470 --> 01:14:41,910
First thing I feel is we need to make peace with the fact.

922
01:14:41,910 --> 01:14:45,430
that the old education paradigm where.

923
01:14:45,430 --> 01:14:47,189
we study for a few years you know school.

924
01:14:47,189 --> 01:14:49,590
and college and then coast through the rest of our career.

925
01:14:49,590 --> 01:14:53,350
So that one is gone.

926
01:14:53,350 --> 01:14:56,630
So we definitely have to be lifelong learners.

927
01:14:56,630 --> 01:15:00,229
and at the same time we also need to accept.

928
01:15:00,229 --> 01:15:05,430
that we cannot stay on top of everything and you know.

929
01:15:05,430 --> 01:15:08,870
because the and the other thing is it might not be important to do.

930
01:15:08,870 --> 01:15:14,149
that the halflife of knowledge has become so short.

931
01:15:14,149 --> 01:15:16,229
that there actually is no point learning a lot of things.

932
01:15:16,229 --> 01:15:20,870
that we are not going to use right away because it's anyway going to change.

933
01:15:20,870 --> 01:15:27,990
So what seems to matter a lot more now is figuring out how to learn and adapt.

934
01:15:27,990 --> 01:15:34,870
And if you just look online, there's a lot of noise and very little good signal.

935
01:15:34,870 --> 01:15:39,270
And so it's important for us to focus on number one,

936
01:15:39,280 --> 01:15:44,229
what do we really want to acquire in terms of knowledge, right?

937
01:15:44,229 --> 01:15:52,149
So it helps to curate some trustworthy sources could be newsletters could be people authoritative people.

938
01:15:52,149 --> 01:15:54,870
that you follow or some forums that you participate in.

939
01:15:54,870 --> 01:15:58,149
So curation of sources is important.

940
01:15:58,149 --> 01:16:04,229
The second one is having a mechanism to sample what's going on.

941
01:16:04,229 --> 01:16:06,390
and this could be you know a periodic activity.

942
01:16:06,390 --> 01:16:11,669
In my case, just a few minutes a day, I just look through TLDDR and.

943
01:16:11,669 --> 01:16:17,910
some LinkedIn posts and that gives me a sense of what new things are coming up.

944
01:16:17,910 --> 01:16:22,630
And even if I don't have the bandwidth to really deep dive there,

945
01:16:22,630 --> 01:16:26,390
I just kind of like bookmark it.

946
01:16:26,390 --> 01:16:31,830
for later and maybe once a week I go back to look at some of the interesting things.

947
01:16:31,830 --> 01:16:34,709
Now apart from this I do deep dive into topics.

948
01:16:34,709 --> 01:16:38,070
that I'm really curious about or I'm going to work on soon.

949
01:16:38,070 --> 01:16:44,870
And one more thing that's important is there's a lot out there that's not being peer reviewed.

950
01:16:44,870 --> 01:16:48,310
So we really have to be critical in how we assess the information that's coming to us.

951
01:16:48,310 --> 01:16:53,510
You know there might be great ideas there might be.

952
01:16:53,510 --> 01:16:58,710
also flawed ideas and it's important us to for us to have our thinking caps on in terms. of tooling.

